  "question": {
    "text": "The engine of a train moving with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;towards a platform sounds a whistle at frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The frequency heard by a passenger inside the train is: (Neglect air speed. Speed of sound in air <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>330</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
