  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the frequency of the sound as heard by the passenger inside the train can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>O</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Since the passenger is inside the train, the speeds of the source and the observer are the same.</p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (1) to get the required frequency.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>400</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>330</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>330</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>",
